IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hca-dates`

-- Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) -- the rules the two seats share: the s 3 definitions (health service, general health
-- service, party), who may complain and about what (ss 5, 6, 7), the time for complaining to the Commissioner (s 8), the
-- general code of conduct for general health services (Schedule 2, s 154) clause by clause, the provider's duties with
-- deadlines run as regulative rules (ss 35, 39, 41, 52, 58), and the table of offences and penalties.
--
-- The questions are asked in hca-seat.l4 (the person who received or sought the health service, and others who
-- complain) and hca-seat-provider.l4 (the general health service provider), which IMPORT this module. Nothing here is
-- exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "is not entitled",
-- "must not ... unless", "if" conditions that fail, a period the text fixes); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on
-- the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The Commissioner's judgments ("reasonably believes", "is satisfied",
-- "considers appropriate") and the judgments the Act leaves open ("unreasonable", "safe and ethical", "appropriate") are
-- inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Health
-- Complaints Act 2016, Version No. 011 (22 October 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published
-- with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance
-- with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Complaints Act 2016`

§§ `s 3 -- health service, general health service, party`

-- s 3(1) "health service means the following services -- (a) an activity performed in relation to a person that is
-- intended or claimed (expressly or otherwise) by the person or the provider of the service -- (i) to assess, predict,
-- maintain or improve the person's physical, mental or psychological health or status; or (ii) to diagnose ...; or (iii)
-- to prevent or treat the person's illness, injury or disability ...; (b) a health related disability, palliative care or
-- aged care service; (c) a surgical or related service; (d) the prescribing or dispensing of a drug or medicinal
-- preparation; (e) the prescribing or dispensing of an aid or piece of equipment for therapeutic use; (f) health
-- education services; (g) therapeutic counselling and psychotherapeutic services; (h) support services necessary to
-- implement any services referred to in paragraphs (a) to (g); (i) services -- (i) that are ancillary to any other
-- services to which this definition applies; and (ii) that affect or may affect persons who are receiving other
-- services to which this definition applies; (j) any other prescribed services".
DECLARE `Kind of service` IS ONE OF
    `an activity to assess, maintain or improve health, or to diagnose, prevent or treat illness, injury or disability`
    `a health related disability, palliative care or aged care service`
    `a surgical or related service`
    `prescribing or dispensing a drug or medicinal preparation`
    `prescribing or dispensing a therapeutic aid or equipment`
    `a health education service`
    `therapeutic counselling or psychotherapy`
    `a support service needed to carry out one of these`
    `an ancillary service such as laundry, cleaning or catering`
    `a service prescribed by the regulations`
    `none of these`

-- A "means" definition: FALSE where no paragraph applies. Paragraph (i) needs both limbs.
GIVEN `the kind`                                      IS A `Kind of service`
      `the ancillary service affects people receiving health services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- a health service` `the kind` `the ancillary service affects people receiving health services` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an ancillary service such as laundry, cleaning or catering` THEN `the ancillary service affects people receiving health services`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 3(1) "general health service means a health service that is not a health profession service"; "health profession
-- service means the practice of a health profession"; "health profession means a health profession within the meaning of
-- the National Law" (borrowed: asked as a fact). The test is the service, not the person: a registered practitioner
-- providing a service outside the practice of their profession provides a general health service (finding 2).
GIVEN `it is a health service`                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the practice of a National Law health profession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- a general health service` `it is a health service` `it is the practice of a National Law health profession` IF
    `it is a health service` AND (NOT `it is the practice of a National Law health profession`)

-- s 3(1) "party, in relation to a complaint, means -- (a) the complainant; or (b) any health service provider about whom
-- the complaint is made; or (c) the person who received or sought the health service, if that person -- (i) is not the
-- complainant; and (ii) has not notified the Commissioner under section 22 that the person does not wish to be a party".
-- s 22(2): "the person giving the notice is taken not to be a party". A "means" definition: FALSE outside it.
DECLARE `My place in the complaint` IS ONE OF
    `the complainant`
    `the health service provider complained about`
    `the person who received or sought the service, not the complainant`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `my place`                       IS A `My place in the complaint`
      `I notified that I do not wish to be a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- I am a party to the complaint` `my place` `I notified that I do not wish to be a party` IF
    CONSIDER `my place`
    WHEN `the complainant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the health service provider complained about` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the person who received or sought the service, not the complainant` THEN NOT `I notified that I do not wish to be a party`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 5, 6, 7 -- who may complain, about what`

-- The complainant's standing: s 5 (the person who received or sought the service), s 6 (any person, about a service to
-- another person), s 7 (a carer of the person). A carer is also "a person" under s 6 (fork F3).
DECLARE `Who is complaining` IS ONE OF
    `the person who received or sought the service`
    `another person`
    `a carer of the person who received or sought the service`

-- What the complaint is about, as the complainant can state it. Each field is one head of ss 5(1), 6(1), 7(1) or of
-- ss 5(2)(b), 6(2)(b). Whether provision, a failure or a manner was "unreasonable" is the complainant's to state (an
-- input); the Act does not define it.
DECLARE `Complaint facts` HAS
    `the provision of the service was unreasonable`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was an unreasonable failure to provide a service sought`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was an unreasonable failure to act consistently with the health service principles` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the service was provided in an unreasonable manner`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider failed to comply with the duty of candour`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is about how the provider dealt with my complaint to it`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is about how the provider dealt with the patient's own complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider treated me unreasonably as carer`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider treated me unreasonably as carer over the duty of candour` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a general provider failed to comply with a code of conduct or an order` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The four heads ss 5(1) and 6(1) share: (a) unreasonable provision, (b) unreasonable failure to provide a service
-- sought, (c) unreasonable failure to act consistently with the health service principles, (d) unreasonable manner,
-- (da) failure to comply with the duty of candour (Health Services Act 1988 Part 5A).
GIVEN f IS A `Complaint facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a service head of ss 5(1), 6(1)` f IF
       f's `the provision of the service was unreasonable`
    OR f's `there was an unreasonable failure to provide a service sought`
    OR f's `there was an unreasonable failure to act consistently with the health service principles`
    OR f's `the service was provided in an unreasonable manner`
    OR f's `the provider failed to comply with the duty of candour`

-- s 5(1): (a) to (da) above, and (e) "the manner in which a complaint by the person is dealt with by the health service
-- provider". s 6(1): (a) to (da), (e)(i) the person's own complaint, (e)(ii) "a complaint ... made by another person
-- under section 5(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d)" (finding 4: not (da) or (e)). s 7(1): (a) "unreasonable treatment of the
-- carer by the provider when providing or failing to provide a health service to the person cared for", (ab) the same in
-- the course of the duty of candour, (b) the manner in which the carer's own complaint is dealt with. A carer may also
-- complain under s 6 as "a person" (fork F3).
GIVEN `who`  IS A `Who is complaining`
      f      IS A `Complaint facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a head of ss 5(1), 6(1), 7(1)` `who` f IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the person who received or sought the service` THEN
           `a service head of ss 5(1), 6(1)` f
        OR f's `it is about how the provider dealt with my complaint to it`
    WHEN `another person` THEN `a head of s 6(1)` f
    WHEN `a carer of the person who received or sought the service` THEN
           f's `the provider treated me unreasonably as carer`
        OR f's `the provider treated me unreasonably as carer over the duty of candour`
        OR f's `it is about how the provider dealt with my complaint to it`
        OR `a head of s 6(1)` f
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        GIVEN g IS A `Complaint facts`
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `a head of s 6(1)` g MEANS
               `a service head of ss 5(1), 6(1)` g
            OR g's `it is about how the provider dealt with my complaint to it`
            OR g's `it is about how the provider dealt with the patient's own complaint`

-- ss 5(2)(b), 6(2)(b): "any failure by a general health service provider in providing or failing to provide a general
-- health service to the person [another person] -- (i) to comply or act consistently with a code of conduct applying to
-- the general health service; or (ii) to comply with an interim prohibition order; or (iii) to comply with a prohibition
-- order". Not in s 7(2); a carer has it through s 6(2) (fork F3).

-- The route to the Commissioner, ss 5(2), 6(2), 7(2): (a) a head of subsection (1) "without making a complaint to the
-- health service provider, if it would be unreasonable or inappropriate to resolve the matter by making a complaint under
-- subsection (1)"; (b) the code and order head; (c) "a matter that was the subject of a complaint by the person to a
-- health service provider under subsection (1), if that complaint is not resolved within 3 months of making the
-- complaint"; (d) "the manner in which a complaint by the person under subsection (1) is dealt with by the health service
-- provider".
DECLARE `Route facts` HAS
    `it would be unreasonable or inappropriate to complain to the provider first` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I complained to the provider`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day I complained to the provider`     IS A DATE
    `the provider has resolved my complaint`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the provider resolved it`         IS A DATE

-- s 5(2)(c), 6(2)(c), 7(2)(b): "not resolved within 3 months of making the complaint". The 3 months end on the day 3
-- months after the day of the complaint (fork F2); the route opens the next day if the complaint is still unresolved, or
-- was resolved only after that day.
GIVEN r IS A `Route facts`, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provider did not resolve it within 3 months` r `today` IF
        r's `I complained to the provider`
    AND (`today` `is after` `the last day of the 3 months`)
    AND ((NOT r's `the provider has resolved my complaint`) OR (r's `the day the provider resolved it` `is after` `the last day of the 3 months`))
    WHERE
        `the last day of the 3 months` MEANS `the date` 3 `months after` (r's `the day I complained to the provider`)

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who is complaining`, f IS A `Complaint facts`, r IS A `Route facts`, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 5(2), 6(2), 7(2) -- a route to the Commissioner` `who` f r `today` IF
       (`a head of ss 5(1), 6(1), 7(1)` `who` f AND r's `it would be unreasonable or inappropriate to complain to the provider first`)
    OR f's `a general provider failed to comply with a code of conduct or an order`
    OR (`a head of ss 5(1), 6(1), 7(1)` `who` f AND `the provider did not resolve it within 3 months` r `today`)
    OR (r's `I complained to the provider` AND f's `it is about how the provider dealt with my complaint to it`)

-- s 8(1): "A person is not entitled to make a complaint to the Commissioner under section 5(2) or 6(2) and a carer is not
-- entitled to make a complaint to the Commissioner under section 7(2) -- (a) more than 12 months after the provision of
-- the health service was completed; or (b) if the health service was not provided, more than 12 months after the health
-- service was sought." The last day is the day 12 months after (fork F2); the day after is "more than 12 months after".
GIVEN `the service was provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the service was completed` IS A DATE
      `the day the service was sought`    IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8(1) -- the last day to complain to the Commissioner` `the service was provided` `the day the service was completed` `the day the service was sought` MEANS
    IF `the service was provided`
    THEN `the date` 12 `months after` `the day the service was completed`
    ELSE `the date` 12 `months after` `the day the service was sought`

-- The answer to "can I complain to the Commissioner", with s 8(2): "Despite subsection (1), the Commissioner may deal
-- with a complaint lodged after the end of the 12 month period if the Commissioner is satisfied that the circumstances of
-- the case so require." The Commissioner's satisfaction is an input.
DECLARE `Commissioner complaint answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, you may complain to the Commissioner`
    `out of time, but the Commissioner is satisfied the circumstances require it and may deal with it (s 8(2))`
    `no, it is more than 12 months after the service (s 8(1))`
    `not yet on these facts: the Act gives no route to the Commissioner`

§§ `Schedule 2 -- the general code of conduct`

-- s 154(2): "The general code of conduct set out in Schedule 2 applies until a general code of conduct in respect of
-- general health services is prescribed by the regulations." None was found deposited; Schedule 2 is encoded (fork F7).
-- Each clause below answers whether, on the facts, the provider has contravened it: JUST TRUE where a "must" or "must
-- not" is not kept; JUST FALSE where the clause is engaged and kept on every head the facts reach. Clause 1(1) "safe and
-- ethical manner" is an open-ended duty ("Without limiting subclause (1)") and is asked as its own fact. Two clauses say
-- "should" (cl 13(3), cl 16): not kept gives NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording* (fork F8).

-- cl 1 "(1) A general health service provider must provide general health services in a safe and ethical manner. (2)
-- Without limiting subclause (1), ... (a) must maintain the necessary competence in the provider's field of practice; (b)
-- must not provide a health service of a type that is outside the provider's experience or training, or provide services
-- that the provider is not qualified to provide; (c) must only prescribe or recommend treatments or appliances that serve
-- the needs of clients; (d) must recognise the limitations of the treatment the provider can provide and refer clients to
-- other competent health service providers in appropriate circumstances; (e) must recommend to clients that additional
-- opinions and services be sought, where appropriate; (f) must assist a client to find other appropriate health care
-- services, if required and practicable; (g) must encourage clients to inform their treating medical practitioner (if
-- any) of the treatments or care being provided; (h) must have a sound understanding of any possible adverse interactions
-- ... and advise the client of these interactions; (i) must provide general health services in a manner that is culturally
-- sensitive to the needs of the provider's clients."
DECLARE `Clause 1 facts` HAS
    `the service was not provided in a safe and ethical manner`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider lacked the necessary competence`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the service was outside the provider's experience, training or qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider prescribed or recommended something not serving the client's needs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not refer on when that was appropriate`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not recommend another opinion when appropriate`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not help find other services when required and practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not encourage telling the treating doctor`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not advise of possible adverse interactions it knew or should have known of` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the service was not culturally sensitive`                         IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN c IS A `Clause 1 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cl 1 -- contravened` c IF
       c's `the service was not provided in a safe and ethical manner`
    OR c's `the provider lacked the necessary competence`
    OR c's `the service was outside the provider's experience, training or qualifications`
    OR c's `the provider prescribed or recommended something not serving the client's needs`
    OR c's `the provider did not refer on when that was appropriate`
    OR c's `the provider did not recommend another opinion when appropriate`
    OR c's `the provider did not help find other services when required and practicable`
    OR c's `the provider did not encourage telling the treating doctor`
    OR c's `the provider did not advise of possible adverse interactions it knew or should have known of`
    OR c's `the service was not culturally sensitive`

-- cl 2 "Prior to commencing a treatment or service, a general health service provider must ensure that consent
-- appropriate to that treatment or service has been obtained and complies with the laws applying in Victoria."
-- cl 3 "(1) ... must accept the right of the provider's clients to make informed choices ... (2) ... must not attempt to
-- dissuade a client from seeking or continuing medical treatment. (3) ... must communicate and co-operate with colleagues
-- and other health service providers and agencies in the best interests of their clients."
GIVEN `appropriate lawful consent was obtained before starting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cl 2 -- contravened` `appropriate lawful consent was obtained before starting` IF
    NOT `appropriate lawful consent was obtained before starting`

GIVEN `the provider did not accept the client's informed choices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider tried to dissuade the client from medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider did not co-operate with other providers in the client's interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cl 3 -- contravened` `the provider did not accept the client's informed choices` `the provider tried to dissuade the client from medical treatment` `the provider did not co-operate with other providers in the client's interests` IF
       `the provider did not accept the client's informed choices`
    OR `the provider tried to dissuade the client from medical treatment`
    OR `the provider did not co-operate with other providers in the client's interests`

-- cl 4 "A general health service provider who, in the course of providing treatment or care, forms the reasonable belief
-- that another health service provider has placed or is placing clients at serious risk of harm must refer the matter to
-- the Commissioner." The "who"-clause unmet: JUST FALSE (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05). No time is fixed.
GIVEN `I formed a reasonable belief of serious risk from another provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I referred the matter to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cl 4 -- contravened` `I formed a reasonable belief of serious risk from another provider` `I referred the matter to the Commissioner` IF
    `I formed a reasonable belief of serious risk from another provider` AND (NOT `I referred the matter to the Commissioner`)

-- cl 5 "(1) ... must take appropriate and timely measures to minimise harm to clients when an adverse event occurs ...
-- (2) ... (a) ensure that appropriate first aid is available ...; (b) obtain appropriate emergency assistance in the event
-- of any serious adverse event; (c) promptly disclose the adverse event to the client and take appropriate remedial steps
-- to reduce the risk of recurrence; (d) report the adverse event to the relevant authority, where appropriate."
DECLARE `Clause 5 facts` HAS
    `an adverse event occurred`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not take appropriate and timely measures to minimise harm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appropriate first aid was not available`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the event was serious and emergency help was not obtained`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the event was not promptly disclosed to the client, or no remedial steps were taken` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was not reported to the relevant authority where appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 5 is engaged "when an adverse event occurs" ("when" counts as "where": ruling (c) of 2026-11-05); 5(2)(a) (first aid
-- available) is a standing duty and holds with or without an event.
GIVEN c IS A `Clause 5 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cl 5 -- contravened` c IF
       c's `appropriate first aid was not available`
    OR (    c's `an adverse event occurred`
        AND (   c's `the provider did not take appropriate and timely measures to minimise harm`
             OR c's `the event was serious and emergency help was not obtained`
             OR c's `the event was not promptly disclosed to the client, or no remedial steps were taken`
             OR c's `it was not reported to the relevant authority where appropriate`))

-- cl 6 "(1) ... must adopt standard precautions for the control of infection ... (2) ... who carries out skin
-- penetration or other invasive procedures must comply with the laws applying in Victoria."
GIVEN `standard infection precautions were not adopted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `skin penetration or invasive procedures broke Victorian law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cl 6 -- contravened` `standard infection precautions were not adopted` `skin penetration or invasive procedures broke Victorian law` IF
    `standard infection precautions were not adopted` OR `skin penetration or invasive procedures broke Victorian law`

-- cl 7 "(1) A general health service provider who has been diagnosed with a medical condition that can be passed on to
-- clients must practise in a manner that does not put clients at risk. (2) ... must take and follow advice from a suitably
-- qualified registered health practitioner ..." cl 10 "(1) ... must not provide treatment or care to clients while under
-- the influence of alcohol or unlawful substances. (2) ... who is taking prescribed medication must obtain advice from the
-- prescribing health practitioner or dispensing pharmacist ... and must refrain from treating or caring for clients in
-- circumstances where the provider's capacity is or may be impaired." cl 11 "(1) ... must not provide treatment or care
-- to clients while suffering from a physical or mental impairment, disability, condition or disorder (including an
-- addiction ...) that places or is likely to place clients at risk of harm. (2) ... if [the provider] has a mental or
-- physical impairment that could place clients at risk, ... must seek advice from a suitably qualified health practitioner
-- ..."
DECLARE `Provider's health facts` HAS
    `the provider has a transmissible condition`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider practised in a way that put clients at risk of it`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not take and follow a registered practitioner's advice on it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider treated clients under the influence of alcohol or unlawful substances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider takes prescribed medication`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not get advice on its effect`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider treated clients while capacity was or may have been impaired by it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider treated clients with an impairment likely to place them at risk of harm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider has an impairment that could place clients at risk`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not seek advice on it`                                IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN h IS A `Provider's health facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cl 7, 10, 11 -- contravened` h IF
       (h's `the provider has a transmissible condition` AND (h's `the provider practised in a way that put clients at risk of it` OR h's `the provider did not take and follow a registered practitioner's advice on it`))
    OR h's `the provider treated clients under the influence of alcohol or unlawful substances`
    OR (h's `the provider takes prescribed medication` AND (h's `the provider did not get advice on its effect` OR h's `the provider treated clients while capacity was or may have been impaired by it`))
    OR h's `the provider treated clients with an impairment likely to place them at risk of harm`
    OR (h's `the provider has an impairment that could place clients at risk` AND h's `the provider did not seek advice on it`)

-- cl 8 "(1) ... must not claim or represent that the provider is qualified, able or willing to cure cancer or other
-- terminal illnesses. (2) ... who claims to be able to treat or alleviate the symptoms of cancer or other terminal
-- illnesses must be able to substantiate such claims." cl 9 "(1) ... must not engage in any form of misinformation or
-- misrepresentation in relation to the products or services the provider provides or the qualifications, training or
-- professional affiliations the provider holds. (2) ... (a) must not use the provider's possession of a particular
-- qualification to mislead or deceive ...; (b) must provide truthful information as to the provider's qualifications,
-- training or professional affiliations; (c) must not make claims ... about the efficacy of treatment or services ... if
-- those claims cannot be substantiated."
DECLARE `Claims facts` HAS
    `the provider claimed to be able or willing to cure cancer or a terminal illness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider claimed to treat or relieve symptoms of cancer or a terminal illness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider can substantiate that claim`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider misinformed about products, services, qualifications or affiliations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider used a qualification to mislead about competence`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider made efficacy claims it cannot substantiate`              IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN c IS A `Claims facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cl 8, 9 -- contravened` c IF
       c's `the provider claimed to be able or willing to cure cancer or a terminal illness`
    OR (c's `the provider claimed to treat or relieve symptoms of cancer or a terminal illness` AND (NOT c's `the provider can substantiate that claim`))
    OR c's `the provider misinformed about products, services, qualifications or affiliations`
    OR c's `the provider used a qualification to mislead about competence`
    OR c's `the provider made efficacy claims it cannot substantiate`

-- cl 12 "(1) ... must not financially exploit the provider's clients. (2) ... (a) must only provide services or
-- treatments to clients that are designed to maintain or improve clients' health or wellbeing; (b) must not accept or
-- offer financial inducements or gifts as a part of client referral arrangements ...; (c) must not ask clients to give,
-- lend or bequeath money or gifts that will benefit the general health service provider directly or indirectly."
-- cl 13 "(1) ... must not engage in behaviour of a sexual or close personal nature with a client. (2) ... must not engage
-- in a sexual or other inappropriate close personal, physical or emotional relationship with a client. (3) ... should
-- ensure that a reasonable period of time has elapsed since the conclusion of the therapeutic relationship before
-- engaging in a sexual relationship with a client."
DECLARE `Money and conduct facts` HAS
    `the provider financially exploited the client`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider gave services not designed to maintain or improve health or wellbeing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider accepted or offered referral inducements or gifts`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider asked the client to give, lend or bequeath money or gifts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider engaged in sexual or close personal behaviour with a client` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider had a sexual or inappropriate close relationship with a client` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider began a sexual relationship with a former client too soon` IS A BOOLEAN

-- JUST TRUE where a "must" or "must not" of cl 12 or 13(1), (2) is not kept; otherwise NOTHING where only cl 13(3)
-- ("should") is engaged (NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*, fork F8); otherwise JUST FALSE.
GIVEN c IS A `Money and conduct facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`cl 12, 13 -- contravened` c MEANS
    IF     c's `the provider financially exploited the client`
        OR c's `the provider gave services not designed to maintain or improve health or wellbeing`
        OR c's `the provider accepted or offered referral inducements or gifts`
        OR c's `the provider asked the client to give, lend or bequeath money or gifts`
        OR c's `the provider engaged in sexual or close personal behaviour with a client`
        OR c's `the provider had a sexual or inappropriate close relationship with a client`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF c's `the provider began a sexual relationship with a former client too soon`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- cl 14 "... must comply with the relevant privacy laws that apply to clients' health information, including -- (a) the
-- Health Records Act 2001; and (b) the Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014; and (c) the Privacy Act 1988 of the
-- Commonwealth." cl 15 "(1) ... must maintain accurate, legible and up-to-date clinical records for each client
-- consultation and ensure that these are held securely ... (2) ... must take necessary steps to facilitate clients' access
-- to information contained in their health records if requested. (3) ... must facilitate the transfer of a client's
-- health record in a timely manner when requested to do so by the client or the client's legal representative." cl 16
-- "... should ensure that appropriate indemnity insurance arrangements are in place ..." cl 17 "(1) ... must bring each
-- of the following documents to the attention of, or make available a copy of each of the following documents to, the
-- clients ... when providing or offering to provide a general health service -- (a) a copy of this code of conduct; (b) a
-- document that gives information about the way in which clients may make a complaint to the Commissioner. (2) Copies of
-- these documents must be made available in a manner that makes them easily accessible to clients."
DECLARE `Records and information facts` HAS
    `the provider broke a privacy law on the client's health information`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not keep accurate, legible, up-to-date and secure records` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the client asked for access to their records`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not help with that access`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the client or their lawyer asked for the records to be transferred`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not help transfer them in a timely way`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider has no appropriate indemnity insurance`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider did not make the code and the complaints information easily available` IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 15(2) and (3) are engaged "if requested" and "when requested" (JUST FALSE without a request). cl 16 says "should":
-- not kept alone gives NOTHING (fork F8).
GIVEN c IS A `Records and information facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`cl 14 to 17 -- contravened` c MEANS
    IF     c's `the provider broke a privacy law on the client's health information`
        OR c's `the provider did not keep accurate, legible, up-to-date and secure records`
        OR (c's `the client asked for access to their records` AND c's `the provider did not help with that access`)
        OR (c's `the client or their lawyer asked for the records to be transferred` AND c's `the provider did not help transfer them in a timely way`)
        OR c's `the provider did not make the code and the complaints information easily available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF c's `the provider has no appropriate indemnity insurance`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The code reaches only a general health service (s 3 "code of conduct", s 154; ss 5(2)(b), 6(2)(b) "a code of conduct
-- applying to the general health service"). Not a general health service: JUST FALSE (a "means" definition). Otherwise
-- the clause answer as given.
GIVEN `it is a general health service` IS A BOOLEAN, `the clause answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the code answer` `it is a general health service` `the clause answer` MEANS
    IF `it is a general health service` THEN `the clause answer` ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`as an answer` b MEANS IF b THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Duties with deadlines -- the provider's`

DECLARE `What became of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open`
    `not done in time, but with a reasonable excuse (no offence)`

DECLARE `Provider` IS ONE OF
    `the health service provider`

-- s 35(3): "A health service provider to whom a notice is given under this section must comply with the requirements of
-- the notice" (a written response to each issue, "within which the response must be given, which must be no more than 20
-- business days after the notice is given", s 35(2); extendable, s 36). 20 / 100 penalty units.
-- s 41(3): the same for producing documents in a conciliation (s 41(2), extendable, s 42). 20 / 100 penalty units.
-- s 39(3): "must not, without reasonable excuse, contravene the requirement" to report on an undertaking "within the time
-- fixed by the Commissioner", which "must not be more than 12 months after the undertaking is given" (s 39(2)). 60 / 300.
-- s 52: "must not, without reasonable excuse, fail to give a written response to that investigation report ... within the
-- time set out in the investigation report". 60 / 300. s 58: the same for a follow up report. 60 / 300.
DECLARE `Provider's act` IS ONE OF
    `give the Commissioner a written response to each issue (s 35)`
    `report on implementing the undertaking (s 39)`
    `produce the documents or evidence (s 41)`
    `give a written response to the investigation report (s 52)`
    `give a written response to the follow up report (s 58)`

GIVEN `the act` IS A `Provider's act`, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Provider` `Provider's act`
`the provider must do it in time` `the act` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the health service provider`
    MUST EXACTLY `the act`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the health service provider` BECAUSE "the provider did not do what the Commissioner's notice, requirement or report required within the time it set (ss 35, 39, 41, 52, 58 of the Health Complaints Act 2016)"

-- The helper that runs the duty over what happened (in the shape of the Coroners Act 2008 encoding's helper). On the
-- stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED means in
-- time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it now would still be in time.
GIVEN `the act`                     IS A `Provider's act`
      `the days allowed`            IS A NUMBER
      `the act has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done`   IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`                IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of the provider's duty` `the act` `the days allowed` `the act has been done` `the time the act was done` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the provider must do it in time` `the act` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the health service provider` `the act` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the provider must do it in time` `the act` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the health service provider` `the act` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

-- By dates: the duty runs from the day of the notice, requirement or report to the last day it allowed (as extended
-- under s 36 or s 42). "Without reasonable excuse" (ss 39(3), 52, 58) turns a late act into no offence; the excuse (for
-- example under ss 77, 78: self-incrimination, privilege) is an input. ss 35(3) and 41(3) have no excuse words, so a late
-- act stays "not done in time" there (fork F13, finding 8).
GIVEN `the act`                IS A `Provider's act`
      `the day of the notice`  IS A DATE
      `the last day allowed`   IS A DATE
      `it has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was done`    IS A DATE
      `today`                  IS A DATE
      `there is a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of it, by dates` `the act` `the day of the notice` `the last day allowed` `it has been done` `the day it was done` `today` `there is a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    IF `the answer` EQUALS `not done in time` AND `there is a reasonable excuse` AND `the offence has excuse words`
    THEN `not done in time, but with a reasonable excuse (no offence)`
    ELSE `the answer`
    WHERE
        `the offence has excuse words` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the act`
            WHEN `give the Commissioner a written response to each issue (s 35)` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `produce the documents or evidence (s 41)` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the answer` MEANS `what became of the provider's duty` `the act` (`the days from` `the day of the notice` `to` `the last day allowed`) `it has been done` (`the days from` `the day of the notice` `to` `the day it was done`) (`the days from` `the day of the notice` `to` `today`)

§§ `Offences and penalties`

-- The offences a person may meet in a complaint, with the maximum penalty "In the case of a natural person" and "In the
-- case of a body corporate". The value of a penalty unit is fixed under the Monetary Units Act 2004, not deposited: the
-- answer is in penalty units. ss 151, 152 (the Commissioner's staff) are out.
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 35 -- not giving the written response the Commissioner required`
    `s 39 -- not reporting on an undertaking as required`
    `s 41 -- not producing documents required in a conciliation`
    `s 43 -- disclosing what was said, done or agreed in a conciliation`
    `s 52 -- not responding to an investigation report`
    `s 58 -- not responding to a follow up report`
    `s 68 -- hindering or obstructing a search under warrant`
    `s 70 -- not complying with an investigation hearing notice`
    `s 80(1) -- threatening or intimidating someone not to complain`
    `s 80(2) -- dismissing or causing detriment because of a complaint`
    `s 81 -- a false or misleading statement in a process under the Act`
    `s 93 -- not complying with an interim prohibition order`
    `s 98 -- not complying with a prohibition order`
    `s 102 -- providing a service prohibited in another State or Territory`
    `s 129 -- not giving complaint information the Commissioner required`
    `s 150 -- disclosing information gained in an investigation or complaint data review`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`, `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum penalty units for` `the offence` `a body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 35 -- not giving the written response the Commissioner required` THEN `units` 20 100
    WHEN `s 39 -- not reporting on an undertaking as required` THEN `units` 60 300
    WHEN `s 41 -- not producing documents required in a conciliation` THEN `units` 20 100
    WHEN `s 43 -- disclosing what was said, done or agreed in a conciliation` THEN `units` 20 100
    WHEN `s 52 -- not responding to an investigation report` THEN `units` 60 300
    WHEN `s 58 -- not responding to a follow up report` THEN `units` 60 300
    WHEN `s 68 -- hindering or obstructing a search under warrant` THEN `units` 60 300
    WHEN `s 70 -- not complying with an investigation hearing notice` THEN `units` 120 600
    WHEN `s 80(1) -- threatening or intimidating someone not to complain` THEN `units` 60 300
    WHEN `s 80(2) -- dismissing or causing detriment because of a complaint` THEN `units` 60 300
    WHEN `s 81 -- a false or misleading statement in a process under the Act` THEN `units` 60 300
    WHEN `s 93 -- not complying with an interim prohibition order` THEN `units` 240 1200
    WHEN `s 98 -- not complying with a prohibition order` THEN `units` 240 1200
    WHEN `s 102 -- providing a service prohibited in another State or Territory` THEN `units` 240 1200
    WHEN `s 129 -- not giving complaint information the Commissioner required` THEN `units` 10 50
    WHEN `s 150 -- disclosing information gained in an investigation or complaint data review` THEN `units` 60 300
    OTHERWISE 0
    WHERE
        GIVEN `natural` IS A NUMBER, `corporate` IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `units` `natural` `corporate` MEANS IF `a body corporate` THEN `corporate` ELSE `natural`

-- Imprisonment, natural persons only: s 70 "12 months imprisonment", ss 93, 98, 102 "2 years imprisonment" (24 months),
-- each "or both" with the fine. None for a body corporate or the other offences.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`, `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment for` `the offence` `a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `a body corporate`
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `s 70 -- not complying with an investigation hearing notice` THEN 12
         WHEN `s 93 -- not complying with an interim prohibition order` THEN 24
         WHEN `s 98 -- not complying with a prohibition order` THEN 24
         WHEN `s 102 -- providing a service prohibited in another State or Territory` THEN 24
         OTHERWISE 0
